@startuml
actor Administrator
participant "AdminController" as Controller
participant "RouteTemplateService" as Service
participant "AirportRepository" as Airports
participant "FlightScheduleGenerator" as Generator
database MongoDB

Administrator -> Controller: Create or update route template
Controller -> Service: validate and save template
Service -> Airports: verify both airport codes
Airports --> Service: airport records
Service -> MongoDB: upsert route template
Service -> Generator: generateRollingWindow(today, 120)
Generator -> MongoDB: read active templates
Generator -> Generator: select operating dates\nand convert local times by IANA zones
Generator -> MongoDB: unordered upsert by templateId:date\n(setOnInsert only)
MongoDB --> Generator: write result
Generator --> Service: generated candidates
Service --> Controller: saved route template
Controller --> Administrator: template response

note over Generator,MongoDB
Daily extension repeats the rolling-window generation.
Existing flights are not overwritten or deleted.
end note
@enduml
